From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:39:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 88/88] dspark: every statics staging region starts
 int64-aligned

A DSpark pass stages its statics (int64 [len64] then int32 [len32]) in its own
pinned region; region g starts at g * region_bytes. region_bytes was
8 * len64 + 4 * len32, which is 4 mod 8 whenever len32 is odd (a 12-slot pass at
dspark_block 5, window 128: 34,020 bytes), so every odd region started
misaligned. Up to 12 live asks run one pass in region 0 and never noticed. With
16 slots, groups() splits 13 or 14 live asks into [0,7) and [7,..): the second
pass stages in region 7 and statics() panicked with "incorrect alignment" on
both ranks.

Dev.regionBytes pads a region to int64 alignment; both Dev.init callers use it.
The test checks every region of a 16-slot staging buffer.
---
